      "writtenOn": "2021-12-07T12:24:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This style of variable use is inconsistent throughout this script.\n\n1. \"possible $protects_against_word_splitting context\"\n\n2. ${protects_against_a_following_underscore_or_word_character}\n\n3. \"this ${does_both}\"\n\nYou will very rarely need to protect against following characters.\n\nYou should almost always protect against splitting (it saves readers checking to see if the variable could have whitespace). You can use array variables for cases where you have lists.\n\nAdditionally, word splitting cannot happen to the RHS of an assignment (FOO\u003dbar), but other kinds of expansion can. You can use single quotes to emphasise the static nature of RHS constants.\n\nPlease adjust. Thanks.",
